commit 03c60ac900801c1e3d40d8a46f2d9a81f9a5f734

C03: a corrupted character in «p?gina» still names a public destination, and a navigation final cites only the navigated address (WEB1479)

WEB1477 measured two defects. «Abre la p?gina oficial de OpenAI» (a corrupted character from the transcription) never reached `_symbolic_web_destination`, so the product ran nothing and said it could not open the page: the site-role noun now reads `p[aá?]gina`. The Wikipedia variant navigated to www.wikipedia.org and the final cited another search result («es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia») as the visited address: `compose_visible_defect` now vetoes (`wrong_address`) any URL in a verified-navigation final that is not requestedUrl/finalUrl, with a retry hint to cite only seen.finalUrl.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


